# --- WorkWith environment ---
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in values. NEVER commit `.env`.

# Local prototype uses SQLite (zero setup).
DATABASE_URL="file:./dev.db"

# Secret used to sign session cookies. Generate a long random string, e.g.:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64url'))"
SESSION_SECRET="change-me-to-a-long-random-string"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOING TO PRODUCTION (Supabase Postgres + Supabase Auth)
# See README "From local prototype to hosted app". In short:
#   1. Create a Supabase project, then set:
#        DATABASE_URL="postgresql://...supabase.co:5432/postgres?schema=public"
#   2. Change prisma/schema.prisma datasource provider to "postgresql".
#   3. Swap the local password auth for Supabase Auth (documented seam in src/lib/auth.ts).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
